_kind":"axiom","source_ref":"core/organ_atlas.json::organs[ring2_premise_retrieval_precision_recall_harness].axiom_refs"},{"basis":"authored_atlas_row","component_id":"spatial_world_model_counterfactual_simulation_replay","ref_kind":"axiom","source_ref":"core/organ_atlas.json::organs[spatial_world_model_counterfactual_simulation_replay].axiom_refs"},{"basis":"authored_atlas_row","component_id":"tactic_portfolio_availability_probe","ref_kind":"axiom","source_ref":"core/organ_atlas.json::organs[tactic_portfolio_availability_probe].axiom_refs"},{"basis":"authored_atlas_row","component_id":"target_shape_tactic_routing_gate","ref_kind":"axiom","source_ref":"core/organ_atlas.json::organs[target_shape_tactic_routing_gate].axiom_refs"},{"basis":"authored_atlas_row","component_id":"undeclared_library_prior_symbol_classifier","ref_kind":"axiom","source_ref":"core/organ_atlas.json::organs[undeclared_library_prior_symbol_classifier].axiom_refs"},{"basis":"authored_atlas_row","component_id":"verifier_lab_execution_spine","ref_kind":"axiom","source_ref":"core/organ_atlas.json::organs[verifier_lab_execution_spine].axiom_refs"},{"basis":"authored_atlas_row","component_id":"verifier_lab_kernel","ref_kind":"axiom","source_ref":"core/organ_atlas.json::organs[verifier_lab_kernel].axiom_refs"}],"cited_by_count":29,"component_ids":["annex_knowledge_routing","bounded_autonomy_campaign_packet","bridge_campaign_dag_validation","certificate_kernel_execution_lab","derived_fact_provider_runtime","egress_self_compliance_audit","finite_erdos_denominator_certificate_strike","formal_evidence_cell_anchor_resolver","formal_math_lean_proof_witness","formal_math_premise_retrieval","formal_math_readiness_gate","formal_math_verifier_trace_repair_loop","generated_projection_drift_runtime","lean_proof_search_lab_runtime","lean_std_premise_index","materials_chemistry_closed_loop_lab_safety_replay","mathematical_strategy_atlas_hypothesis_scorer","metabolism_queue_reconciliation","navigation_fitness_benchmark","proof_diagnostic_evidence_spine","provider_context_recipe_budget_policy","research_replication_rubric_artifact_replay","ring2_premise_retrieval_precision_recall_harness","spatial_world_model_counterfactual_simulation_replay","tactic_portfolio_availability_probe","target_shape_tactic_routing_gate","undeclared_library_prior_symbol_classifier","verifier_lab_execution_spine","verifier_lab_kernel"],"exposed_count":0,"exposure":[],"failure_modes":["AP-2","AP-15"],"id":"AX-2","kind":"axiom","plain":"Formal clause: trusted claims are decided by a small checker `K` over certificates `c`; producers emit certificates and the checker decides.","principles":["P-3"],"reader":{"analogy":{"boundary":"The desk only decides entry for the passes it checks; whether its list is complete is a separate question.","maps":[{"analogy":"the front desk that checks the pass and decides entry","doctrine":"the small separate checker that decides"},{"analogy":"the person who printed the pass, who cannot approve their own entry","doctrine":"the producer of the certificate, which has no say in the decision"},{"analogy":"the pass presented at the desk","doctrine":"the certificate the checker reads"},{"analogy":"you get only as far as the desk has checked, however official the pass looks","doctrine":"a claim is as strong as what the checker examined"}],"text":"At a secure building, the person who printed a visitor pass cannot let themselves in. A small front desk checks the pass against its own list and decides who enters."},"basis":"authored_reader_enrichment","counterexample":"A generator's own confidence is taken as the verdict, so a large producer approves its own output and the small checking step is skipped because the output looked authoritative.","does_not_prove":"A checker accepting one certificate shows only that this certificate passed this checker, and says nothing about the producer's other output or about bugs in the checker itself.","enforced_in_component_ids":["certificate_kernel_execution_lab","formal_math_lean_proof_witness","verifier_lab_kernel"],"example":{"component_ids":["certificate_kernel_execution_lab","formal_math_lean_proof_witness"],"text":"The certificate kernel lab keeps the code that emits certificates separate from a small checker that decides them. A companion Lean example is compiled by the real Lean verifier, whose kernel rejects an invalid proof whatever the producer intended."},"governs":"Which part decides a claim: the small checker, never the producer.","plain":"A claim is trusted only when a small, separate check works it out again from the evidence supplied with it. The program that produced an answer never approves its own answer, however capable it is.","potential_misread":"That a powerful, confident producer can vouch for its own output, so the small separate check can be skipped when the output looks authoritative.","refuses":"Trusting the producer in place of the checker.","requires":"A small checker that decides by reading a certificate, kept separate from the program that produced it.","source_ref":"core/doctrine_enrichment.json","why_it_matters":"The part someone has to audit stays small and fixed while the programs generating answers grow larger and faster."},"rests_on":[],"source_ref":"AXIOMS.md::AX-2","statement":"Formal clause: trusted claims are decided by a small checker `K` over\ncertificates `c`; producers emit certificates and the checker decides.\n\nLineage: de Bruijn criterion, LCF/Lean kernel architecture, proof by reflection.\n\nRoute: recorded as strongly witnessed by `certificate_kernel_execution_lab`,\n`formal_math_lean_proof_witness`, the Crown Jewel common harness and the\ngenerated Lean certificate modules. The tests feed in invalid proof witnesses\nand require the checker to reject them.\n\nAnti-axiom: trust in whoever produced a result stands in for a check.","statement_sha256":"d1f94ec7184396b11f44dca991295fc80c82254e7b1b78e5d4945be32b0c8f4d","title":"Kernelized verification","violates":[]},"schema_version":"plectis_component_http_v1","snapshot_revision":"45be1deb333ad57cd9ae093229455d0a52d3bf23a9064cde09f1a6e16f4c7044"}